Z||000000||kel||01-18-2000||12:43 AM||||Some of you may remember a little while back I had a leak in the heater core.  The foggy windows, you turn it up, it gets worse...you finally figure out what it is (thanks to this forum), but by that time the vapor had loosened the headliner.  It started sagging to the point it was almost laying on my head.  Got the headliner replaced last week, looks good.  Then, I'm going through the carwash and my antenna breaks off.  Getting that replaced Thursday.  Until 1999, I barely had a scratch on my car, now leaky heater cores, sagging headliners, broken antennas, dented noses (accident), funky steering...they are all fixed or will be soon (except the funky steering), but do you think we could just rewind to 1998?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  ||||reg||7
Z||000001||DXR_DAD||01-18-2000||12:58 AM||||What's up Kel,<P>Who did your headliner and what was the price? I just did the headliner on my 87coupe it came out real good if I say so myself I did get the visors done at a local shop. Hourly rate $55.00. It cost me $11.00.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Patrick||01-18-2000||01:42 AM||||<BR>I've heard of car antennas being snapped off at car washes, getting stuck in the revolving brush, and then thrashing the heck out of the car's paint job. I hope that didn't happen to you Kel.||||reg||4
Z||000003||kel||01-18-2000||01:52 AM||||Hi DXR_DAD,<BR>I had a local guy do it, Secrest's Auto Upholstery.  Two different guys I spoke to had recommended him (one was a guy from the parts dept. of my local Pontiac dealership, who also happens to own a 87 Fiero GT)  Anyway, he did a good job.  To replace the headliner and redo the visors it cost $120.00.<P>Hey Patrick,<BR>I thought about that as soon as I saw the antenna was gone, so I checked, but didn't see any scratches.||||reg||1
